  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Workshop Circular Economy Summit</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh&apos;s apparel and textile industry has achieved significant success as a global garments manufacturer, but at a high environmental cost. The industry&apos;s exponential growth has resulted in waste generation, resource depletion, and pollution.Embracing circular economy principles offers a compelling solution to these challenges, by transitioning from a linear model to one that promotes resource efficiency and waste reduction. Closing the loop through recycling, reusing, and designing for durability can yield numerous benefits. However, investment, technology and effective policy interventions are crucial to drive this transformation and support more circular business models.During, the second Bangladesh Circular Economy Summit (June 2024) these drivers for a transformation towards a more circular apparel and textile industry in Bangladesh will be explored with key industry stakeholders.The Netherlands, via its embassy in Dhaka and The Hague School of Applied Science/Universiteit Groningen, will participate in the Summit by organizing a workshop around Bangladesh-Netherlands collaboration in the circular textile industry.Purpose of the workshop is to teach participants about circularity in the textile industry (and sharing Dutch best practices) and to identify (how the Netherlands can play a role in filling) the current knowledge/technology/policy gaps in Bangladesh&apos;s textile industry and show the necessity to make the sector more circular.</narrative>
  </description>
